Under the hypotheses of Theorem~\ref{thm:sphere}, fix positive width
caps \(a_i\). Then
\begin{equation}
 \lim_{N\to\infty}
 \frac{1}{N}\max_{\mathbf h:\,w_N(h_i)\le a_i}
            H_{\mathbf x}(C(\mathbf h;\mathbf z))
 = \inf_{o\in X}\sum_i a_i d(o,x_i).
\end{equation}
Convergence is uniform over all placements of bounded scale.

There is a valued price $p$ of scale $D$ on $K$ extending $H$. On tensors
with entries in $E[t^{\mathbb Q}]$ it is given by
\begin{equation}
 p(T)=\lim_{n\to\infty}\frac1n
       \max_{j\in\mathbb Q}\bigl(H([t^j]T^{\otimes n})-j\bigr).
\end{equation}
